# v6 parity load table -- generated by mkparity.py from a regdump diff.py
# capture (regdump-v6-vs-s7.txt)
# odi_switch_init_parity()'s loadable table format (odi_switch_dal.c/.h,
# "parity table from a file"):
# one comment line naming the register, then one data line
# "offset value mask name" (hex, no 0x prefix), in the diff's own order.
# 39 entries (25 excluded: snapshot latches, thermal, SerDes windows, PTP and EPON state that move on their own)
# Register names relabelled to ours (regnames.txt, or the address default); offsets, values and masks as generated.
